The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
// Omitted include directive
// extern const u32 vsc7514_ana_regmap[];
// extern const u32 vsc7514_qs_regmap[];
```
Reason:
The omission of the `#include <soc/mscc/ocelot_vcap.h>` directive in the `vsc7514_regs.h` file resulted in unresolved dependencies for the definitions that rely on the contents of `ocelot_vcap.h`, which was not included, causing compilation errors.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
#include <soc/mscc/ocelot_vcap.h>
```
Reason:
Adding the `#include <soc/mscc/ocelot_vcap.h>` directive ensures that the necessary definitions and dependencies from `ocelot_vcap.h` are available in `vsc7514_regs.h`, resolving the compilation issues and allowing the code to function correctly.

